<title>UK: Airtours chief to set up base in U.S.-paper.</title>
<headline>Airtours chief to set up base in U.S.-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airtours Plc chairman and founder will move to America to oversee the company's international expansion programme, the Times said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The paper quoted an Airtours spokesman saying, &quot;Mr. Crossland is going overseas to develop Airtours' business over there....It shows that Airtours is not just a UK tour operator anymore.&quot;</p>
<p>Crossland, who will be based in California, is to reverse the decline in the company's North American operations. He also will look for acquisitions, the paper said. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
